## Research references

Reviewed 2026-09-19. These are engineering and evaluation references, not evidence
that a strategy will be profitable. Adopt patterns incrementally; do not replace
the repository or add these platforms as dependencies.

| Reference | Pattern to apply |
|---|---|
| [QuantConnect LEAN fill models](https://www.quantconnect.com/docs/v2/writing-algorithms/reality-modeling/trade-fills/key-concepts) | Separate strategy decisions from execution; model fill quantity, spread and slippage consistently. |
| [Freqtrade lookahead analysis](https://docs.freqtrade.io/en/latest/lookahead-analysis/) | Check whether removing future data changes earlier signals. |
| [Freqtrade recursive analysis](https://docs.freqtrade.io/en/latest/recursive-analysis/) | Check indicator stability across different warm-up histories. |
| [OpenAlgo sandbox](https://docs.openalgo.in/new-features/api-analyzer) | Separate simulation/live modes and expose orders and operator controls; use our configured capital, not its large default sandbox balance. |
| [Deflated Sharpe Ratio research](https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.2460551) | Preserve multiple-testing penalties rather than selecting the best backtest. |
| [FYERS tariff](https://fyers.in/charges-list) | Version applicable charges and verify against contract notes; free API access does not mean free trading. |

## Implementation progress, in dependency order

The repository utilities below are implemented and tested where stated. External
evidence and integration gates remain open; implementation is not qualification.

### 1. Reliable session data

- Implemented: immutable one-session exports with event ordering, instrument-master,
  explicit intraday corporate-action policy, freshness, quality and content hashes.
- Integrated: the persistent recorder supervisor recognizes configured session
  boundaries, weekends and reviewed holidays, reports the next opening, preserves a
  same-day manual stop and bounds crash restarts. The broker's market status is the
  final paper-fill gate. Missing/wrong-year calendars fail closed.
- Integrated: shadow replay accepts and fully revalidates the exported artifact.
- Implemented: bounded FYERS daily-history artifacts, NIFTY 50 regime history,
  automatic official bhavcopy refresh and post-close finalization. Decisions use
  completed bars only; observation dates are reviewed NSE sessions.
- Completion gate: exported sessions reproduce decisions and quality metrics.
  Unit fixtures pass; a representative market-hours export remains externally pending.

### 2. Shared execution economics

- Implemented: a shared FYERS fill estimator covers whole lots, fee-inclusive cash
  reservation, displayed-liquidity full/partial/unfilled outcomes, adverse slippage
  and tick rounding. Paper and shadow use it; the tariff is effective-date versioned.
  T+1 obligations are recorded with explicit holiday inputs, and session quality
  measures exchange-to-receive latency.
- Implemented: FIFO tax lots/holding periods, versioned tax and infrastructure
  scenarios, break-even-capital reporting and read-only normalized FYERS ledger
  reconciliation. Qualification requires positive passive-benchmark excess after
  these scenarios.
- Remaining: market-measured latency calibration and FYERS historical-backtest
  accounting parity. Reconcile tariff calculations against contract notes;
  preserve historical broker/cost assumptions rather than relabelling old results.
- Completion gate: identical trade sequences produce matching accounting.

### 3. Reproducible strategy research

- Implemented: `research run` exposes an allowlisted real portfolio-backtest adapter
  from hash-registered CSV artifacts. It emits aligned net, benchmark and turnover
  series into the immutable experiment lifecycle; chronological split, bootstrap,
  benchmark and cost-stress reporting use existing validation.
- Implemented: executable lookahead/warm-up analyzers, a point-in-time ISIN-keyed
  bhavcopy adapter, a frozen benchmark, sealed one-time holdout access and auditable
  invalidation of later campaign tuning.
- Register each campaign's hypothesis, parameter budget, benchmark and rejection
  criteria before execution; record every tested configuration.
- Start with an economics audit of existing candidates at the existing ₹10,000
  research assumption. Retest rejected ideas only when new data or a documented
  correction justifies it; retain the original failures and historical conclusions.
- Completion gate: reproduce a registered experiment through the CLI. Strategy
  advancement additionally requires net-of-cost evidence passing unchanged K-60;
  a positive backtest or completed research tooling is not qualification.

### 4. Qualification and forward shadow

- Implemented: qualification binds reviewed code, configuration, data, costs and
  trial-registry hashes; changes block entries. Shadow reports fill rate, missed
  intents, turnover, execution shortfall and drawdown.
- Implemented: a qualification- and halt-gated, idempotent target-to-intent scheduler
  emits auditable paper intents without broker access. The recorder consumes qualified
  rebalance/exit intents through the same paper-fill path. Synthetic engineering
  replay is not deployment.
- Integrated: an observation-only continuous candidate lab records immutable,
  non-overlapping momentum/reversal decisions from fresh FYERS quotes and evaluates
  spread/fee-aware forward returns against a benchmark. It expires missed horizons,
  exposes metrics on the dashboard and has no path to intents or broker mutations.
  These observations are research input, not qualification.
- Implemented: a versioned 20-stock forward universe, lagged broad-market regime
  gate, predeclared momentum/breakout/residual-reversal families, frozen
  lower-confidence-bound selection and whole-share ₹10,000 sizing. Unsafe regimes,
  evidence ties and unqualified families resolve to cash. The registered NSE
  adapter uses next-bar timing, FYERS delivery costs and configurable spread stress.
- Completion gate: reviewed qualification plus forward evidence and replay/forward
  decision parity. A fixed number of paper-trading days alone is insufficient.

### 5. Broker reliability and usable operations

- Implemented behind the disabled transport: throttled submissions, durable
  cancel/modify, trade-ID deduplication and order/trade consistency checks. UNKNOWN
  submissions still require reconciliation. Integrity-checked backups and a
  fail-closed readiness/alert report are exposed through the CLI.
- Implemented: REST broker cash/holding/day-position reconciliation blocks entries
  and persists a halt on divergence. The FYERS-only dashboard presents recorder,
  account, quote, accounting, position, order, settlement, evidence and alert state,
  with authenticated recorder/backup/halt controls. Remaining: streaming order updates.
- Implemented: a verified direct-dependency lock, retained daily backups, isolated
  restore drills, strict preflight, auth-required state, bounded finalization and an
  idempotent Azure installer/systemd deployment. Remaining: operator deployment of
  Azure Monitor email/VM backup and a checked manual release. Logs continue to
  use existing secret-safe boundaries.
- Completion gate: crash, timeout, partial-fill and reconnect drills pass;
  qualified strategy, forward evidence and an accepted loss budget are required
  before separately authorized live deployment.

## Verification and defaults

Each implementation batch requires focused tests, relevant regression tests,
critical lint and whitespace checks. Include replay determinism, accounting parity,
future-data isolation, warm-up stability, evidence invalidation, duplicate fills,
ambiguous submissions and restart/restore scenarios in the relevant batches.

Keep implemented utilities, integrated workflows and externally verified behavior
distinct in status reporting. Preserve the completed batch above; its recorded
test results are historical verification, not a new test run for this roadmap.
No production behavior or qualification status changes with this documentation update.

Use the existing components; do not recreate the engine, indicators, strategies or
dashboard from the obsolete Delta proposal. Automatic parameter promotion remains
disabled. Market-hours samples, measured costs and strategy qualification require
external evidence and are not completed by passing unit tests.
